{"title":"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Camilla had twice as many blueberry jelly beans as cherry jelly beans. After eating 10 pieces of each kind, she now has three times as many blueberry jelly beans as cherry jelly beans. How many blueberry jelly beans did she originally have?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751cca8d6cbbf8b32c3ea521b7d9f6b288e4063d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 20\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 30\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 40\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote the number of blueberry and cherry jelly beans as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> respectively. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/4934ae4c40d6f0fc684aeed2d9d5491586706a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2c$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/138d02aaf27f0d51f1c42a6857fe2f074c5b3370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-10 = 3(c-10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4da1b005a98ef5b0d2a497047306f845e708f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c-10 = 3c-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407f553fe0e13d106e11399b9865e0a4c9a7be97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=20$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896581592b1ebaffbc135092104d3679bba3e04c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"97\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the problem, we see that 10 less than one of the answer choices must be a multiple of 3 and positive. The only answer choice satisfying this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa97cde8cf03dda74625cbcd3055eff4ace936e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />. We can check that 40 blueberry and 20 cherry jelly beans indeed does work.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the number of jellybeans minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/6379c48cba58821b5fc27f5394d099539056edee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 10 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and positive. Therefore, the number of jellybeans is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06cc069e89ba00917d239f101eb9ada9808a43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;20$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. The only answer choice satisfying this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa97cde8cf03dda74625cbcd3055eff4ace936e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Note (not from original author): The problem asks for the number of blueberry jellybeans, not the total number, so we cannot conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is the answer. There are actually <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> total jellybeans, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of which are blueberry jerrybeans.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QrCSysVHhPU\">https://youtu.be/QrCSysVHhPU</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With new whiteboard at home: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zTGuz6EoBWY?t=774\">https://youtu.be/zTGuz6EoBWY?t=774</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B\">2017 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colsp